            <profile id="5b90-2184-39ec-ac95" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="0641-2ee1-c462-c414" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Equipment: none. The wagons may not move normally, instead they are rolled downhill during the Shooting phase. They must be placed on a hill. A unit of warriors must be within 3" of the wagons to launch them. The wagons move straight ahead 3D6", and are removed when they reach the end of their roll distance, or before that if they hit an obstacle. Any unit in the path suffers D6 S5 impact hits. Large targets; drilled troops may open lanes. Troops fighting behind wagons count as being in soft cover. Highland armies only. (Alexander the Great p.83)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <infoLinks>
