  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="f1c2-bc71-f320-49bd" name="Thracians (Alexander the Great) - List Notes" publicationId="0641-2ee1-c462-c414" hidden="false">
      <description>THRACIANS - BARBARIAN ALLIES &amp; ENEMIES (Alexander the Great, pp.82-83). Percentages are by points. Characters up to 25% (the army must have an Army General), Warriors at least 25%, Cavalry up to 33%, Wagons up to 10%, Allies up to 25%.
The minimum size for a regiment is five models, there is no upper limit. One model in each unit may be upgraded to Leader (+5 pts), and Musician (+5 pts), or Standard bearer (+5 pts). Choose the composition that matches the Army General: Thracian King - Coalition or Getic, Warlord - Highland. Rhomphaia: only Mountain tribesmen may have it (also called Highland); it counts as a halberd, +1 Strength, shieldless.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Thracians - Coalition]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Warriors: at least 25%
  Cavalry: up to 33%
  Wagons: up to 10%
  Odrysian coalition under the Thracian King (p.82): Characters up to 25%, Warriors at least 25%, Cavalry up to 33%. Wagons are not allowed. One Mountain warrior unit may be taken for every two Lowland warrior units in the army (not enforced). One Getae Cavalry unit may be taken for each Noble or Light Cavalry unit. Allies up to 25% (Greek Mercenaries: 0-1 Polemarch, Mercenary Hoplites, Peltasts and Greek Cavalry; or Illyrians) documented only.
[Thracians - Getic]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Warriors: at least 25%
  Cavalry: at least 33%
  Wagons: up to 10%
  The Thracian King as a Getic lord (p.82): the cavalry percentage is raised to at least 33% of the points (the book does not repeat an upper limit; none entered). All cavalry may be armed with bows +3 pts (not built as a separate option). Getae cavalry are unrestricted, but Mountain tribesmen and wagons are not allowed. Getic characters may add a bow +4 pts, gain Parthian shot and Feigned flight, raising their cost by +10 pts. Allies up to 25% documented only.
[Thracians - Highland]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Warriors: at least 25%
  Cavalry: up to 25%
  Wagons: up to 10%
  A Warlord as Army General - a Highland Thracian army such as the unruly Bessi (p.82): Cavalry up to 25%, and no Noble or Getae cavalry. One Lowland warrior unit may be taken for every two Mountain warrior units (not enforced). Wagons up to 10%. Allies up to 25% documented only.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
